From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Mon, 10 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: use duelist helpers in field.cpp

Change the two-player sites of field.cpp to the duelist helpers.
With 2 duelists every changed line gives the same result as before.

Changed (34 sites, 2 explicit pairs):
- 5 loops over duelists: bound p < 2 becomes p < n_duelists
  (reload_field_info, adjust_self_destroy_set (2), get_overlay_group,
  get_overlay_count). Order and body stay the same.
- 1 turn-player-first loop: p = 1 - p becomes next_in_turn_order(p)
  (adjust_self_destroy_set). The order stays the same.
- 6 validity checks: uplayer < 2 (3), uplayer > 1 (1) and
  self != 0 && self != 1 (2) become is_duelist / !is_duelist.
  The accepted set is 0 and 1 in both forms. The argument types are
  uint8_t or uint32_t, so no negative value can occur.
- 20 sites with 1 - x become opponent_of(x). The value x is the index of
  player[x] or unique_cards[x] at the site, a card controler, or a value
  that a Lua caller checked to be 0 or 1. Sites where the result goes into
  a uint8_t give the same value for every x.
- 2 local arrays target_player[2] become target_player[MAX_DUELISTS] = {}.
  In each place the two "if(target_player[0]) ... if(target_player[1])" message blocks
  become one loop over n_duelists (2 explicit pairs). The message bytes and their order stay
  the same.

Left unchanged (list in unchanged-sites.md):
- relative self/opponent loops (p < 2 with location1, location2 or
  s_range, o_range or self, oppo): 6. Phase 2 decides the meaning.
- 1 - sumplayer: 1 (decision needed).
- zone flag math (shifts by 16, 11 - sequence, 0xC000 << 16, pzone
  flags): 6 (decision needed, zone ABI).
- constructor options.team1 and options.team2: 1 (needs options change).
- sequence < 2 and pzone i < 2 (not players), PLAYER_NONE checks,
  count - 1 - i: not player sites.
- Loops inside a comment block (save_lp_cost, restore_lp_cost): 2.
